`run` against a transport that will not come up is the act failing — exit 1 —
and stays distinct from a config this tool refuses (2). The fixture is the
same dead client-mode bus zenctl's corpus uses: `connect.timeout_ms: 0`,
`exit_on_failure: true`, so the failure is immediate and without retry.

```console
$ zenwatch run --config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus-run.json5 --once --dry-run
? 1
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!

```
